  "text": "Foster Hospital for Small Animals | Cummings School of Veterinary Medicine\nSkip to main content\nCummings School of Veterinary Medicine\nHenry and Lois Foster Hospital for Small Animals\nHospitals & Clinics\nFoster Hospital for Small Animals\nHospital for Large Animals\nLuke and Lily Lerner Clinic\nTufts Veterinary Field Service\nTufts Wildlife Clinic\nTufts at Tech\nVeterinary Diagnostic Laboratory\nFaculty\nGive\nOpen search\nClose search\nOpen menu\nClose menu\nHenry and Lois Foster Hospital for Small Animals\nAbout\nAAHA Accreditation\nAnnouncements\nDoctors & Staff\nLeadership\nPolicies\nSpecialty & Services\nEmergency Care\nVeterinarian Referrals\nClient Information\nAppointments\nClient Policies\nCounseling and Support\nFAQs\nMedication Refill Request\nPay Invoice\nCummings School of Veterinary Medicine\nHospitals & Clinics\nFoster Hospital for Small Animals\nHospital for Large Animals\nLuke and Lily Lerner Clinic\nTufts Veterinary Field Service\nTufts Wildlife Clinic\nTufts at Tech\nVeterinary Diagnostic Laboratory\nFaculty\nGive\nHome page\nHenry and Lois Foster Hospital for Small Animals\nHenry and Lois Foster Hospital for Small Animals is located in Grafton, Massachusetts, and provides specialty care for dogs, cats, and exotic pets.\nOur wide array of veterinary specialty services are available by appointment only (\n508-839-5395\n) after a referral from a veterinarian.\nHenry and Lois Foster Hospital for Small Animals\nHenry and Lois Foster Hospital for Small Animals is located in Grafton, Massachusetts, and provides specialty care for dogs, cats, and exotic pets.\nOur wide array of veterinary specialty services are available by appointment only (\n508-839-5395\n) after a referral from a veterinarian.\nDo You Have An Emergency?\nEmergency Services are available 24 hours/365 days a year to help you and your pet. If your pet has an emergency, please call prior to coming to the hospital.\n508-839-5395 (Option 3)\nPay Invoice\nPay with Care Credit\nMedication Refill Request\nNew to Foster Hospital?\nHow to make an appointment\nNeed to Refer a Client?\nReferring a client to Foster Hospital is easy\nLooking for a Specialist?\nMeet our board-certified veterinary specialists\nBlood Bank\nFoster Hospital for Small Animals relies upon our generous dog and cat blood donors to provide life-saving blood transfusions to our patients.\nLearn More\nClinical Trials\nFaculty and staff of Cummings School's hospital and clinics have the potential to improve quality of life for your pet by providing them with diagnostics and treatments that are still exploratory and otherwise not available.\nLearn More\nFeatured Stories\nAcid Reflux in Dogs: Causes, Symptoms, and Treatments\nAssociate clinical professor Michael Stone is quoted in AKC Gazette on acid reflux in dogs\nFoster Hospital’s ECC Team Springs into Action to Save Golden Retriever\nThree additional services jump in to treat Goose, bleeding out from an internal injury\nThis Super Common Dog Owner Habit May Be Shaving Years Off Your Pet's Life\nAssociate clinical professor Michael Stone is quoted throughout this article on the risks of obesity for dogs and how to help them lose weight\nMeet Christopher Rego\nChristopher Rego, Biomedical Equipment Technician at Foster Hospital for Small Animals\nCardiology and Oncology Services Pool Expertise to Save Boston Terrier\nArnie’s heart base tumor had shrunk by 70 percent after stenting and radiation therapy\nSummer Tips for Pet Owners\nKeeping pets safe while still having fun\nContact\nHenry and Lois Foster Hospital for Small Animals\n55 Willard Street\nNorth Grafton, MA 01536\nMain:\n508-839-5395\nEmergency Number:\n508-839-5395 (option 3)\nFax:\n508-839-7951\nPharmacy:\n508-887-4850\nDirections & Parking\nFooter\nAccreditation\nAnnual Safety Report\nCareers\nComing to Campus\nDirectory\nWebster Family Library\nHospitals & Clinics\nFoster Hospital for Small Animals\nHospital for Large Animals\nLuke and Lily Lerner Clinic\nTufts Veterinary Field Service\nTufts Wildlife Clinic\nTufts at Tech\nVeterinary Diagnostic Laboratory\nContact\nCummings School of Veterinary Medicine at Tufts University\nJean Mayer Administration Building\n200 Westboro Road\nNorth Grafton, MA 01536\n© Tufts University 2026\nNon-Discrimination Statement\nPrivacy\nTufts Mobile",
